                  crimeit = α − β1 × didit + β2 × postit + ui + λt + εit                                                                                   (8)

     In the above formula, i represents the country, t represents the year; crimeit is the
explained variable, i.e., the cybercrime rate of country i in year t; is the constant term;
1 is the policy effect, didit is the core explanatory variable, which is the interaction term
of the country dummy variable and the time dummy variable, and is used to represent
the dummy variables of different GCI indicators; 2 is the coefficient, postit is the control
variable at the cybercrime level; i represents the fixed effect of country i, t represents
the time fixed effect of year t; εit is the random disturbance term of the multi-period
DID regression model.


